{"number": 140, "text": "           22.1    1 setmenu           4 ready meals\n                   2 food additives    5 fresh produce (Fresh food is also a possible collocation.)\n                   3 junk food\n          22.2     1 Foodadditives     4 fresh produce\n                  2  Junk food         5 set menu\n                  3  ready meals\n          2252    1  Searlétt   4  Bella\n                  2  Michael    5  Layla\n                  3  Logan      6  Connor\n          22.4    1  Processed foods may  damage  our health in the long term.\n                  2  Some  people always have three decent meals a day, but | prefer a hearty breakfast and then a\n                     light meal around midday and a more substantial meal in the evening.\n                  3  There are some overpriced restaurants in the city centre, but down at the beach, there are some\n                     nice, reasonably priced ones.\n                  4  On my birthday my parents took me out for a slap-up meal. They wanted to go for a gourmet\n                     meal but ! said I’d prefer something more ordinary.\n                  5  Ice tea is a refreshing drink on a hot day, and is probably better for you than soft drinks such as\n                    cola or lemonade.\n                  6  Let me take you out to dinner on your birthday. Or would you prefer a home-cooked meal? | could\n                    make  dinner for you at my place.\n\n                  Unit  23\n         23.1     Matthew:    Have you downloaded  that new e-book that has just come out about Ireland?\n                  Camilla:    No, | don’t use my e-book reader app much and | don’t visit websites with book\n                              reviews. What’s it about?\n                  Matthew:         it deals with the Irish War of Independence. It’s very authentic and it manages to\n                              capture the atmosphere  of Ireland at the beginning of the 20th century.\n                  Camilla:    Is it just historical facts, then?\n                  Matthew:    _No, the central characters are two brothers who have different opinions about the war\n                              and this divides their family. In the opening chapters they’re happy and do everything\n                              together, but by the closing chapter they have become enemies.\n                 Camilla:     Mm, it sounds a bit depressing to me.\n                  Matthew:    Well, it certainly doesn’t have a happy ending, but | liked it, and it’s highly\n                              recommended   by ail the critics.\n                 Camilla:    So, a book with a pleasant beginning and a sad end(ing). Not for me, I’m afraid. | prefer\n                             the opposite.\n         23.2    Across             Down\n                 3  absorbed        1  cameo\n                 5  engrossed       2  nominated\n                 6  stage           4 effects\n                 7  lead\n         23.3    full house\n                 bedtime reading\n                 box-office hit\n                 big screen\n                 female lead\n         23.4    1 film                               3 book/magazine/article\n                 2 audiobook / e-book reader app      4 reading\n\n\n  138            English Collocations in Use Intermediate", "char_count": 3284, "mean_conf": 92.8, "word_count": 408, "words": [{"text": "22.1", "x0": 219, "y0": 266, "x1": 318, "y1": 301, "conf": 51, "bold": false}, {"text": "1", "x0": 389, "y0": 276, "x1": 404, "y1": 304, "conf": 67, "bold": false}, {"text": "setmenu", "x0": 438, "y0": 278, "x1": 610, "y1": 308, "conf": 89, "bold": false}, {"text": "4", "x0": 802, "y0": 282, "x1": 822, "y1": 311, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "ready", "x0": 855, "y0": 280, "x1": 959, "y1": 322, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "meals", "x0": 973, "y0": 282, "x1": 1082, "y1": 314, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "2", "x0": 385, "y0": 329, 